#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1076 expect=violation domain=AE
#note "Round 2026-10-15: store-backed (was a declared #library column-order pair, a shape the store never produces). AELAT is an SDTM Model Events-class variable (get_model_column_order) that the SDTMIG 3.4 AE specification does not list (no Req / Exp / Perm row in get_dataset_filtered_variables) -> a model-permissible addition -> fires on AELAT only. The old Check read get_column_order_from_library(), which on the store lists the model class variables too, so it never fired here."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt variable_name=AELAT
#library-ref standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AESEQ   type=Num
col AETERM  type=Char
col AEDECOD type=Char
col AELAT   type=Char
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1 | HEADACHE | Headache | LEFT
---
